    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0381" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9290: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-11T17:00:00+08:00">August 11, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 11—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My August 11, 11 a.m.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d406-f1"/> A Japanese naval vessel is
                    leaving this afternoon for Shanghai carrying all remaining Japanese. The Chinese
                    population of the Japanese Concession which had all previously evacuated will
                    now be permitted to return.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
